# mpd.env — settings for this Astro project.
#
# Edit this file to change how this one project runs. Every setting is
# optional. Leave a line out and mpd uses a default.
#
# Two ways to change a setting:
#
#   mpd start <project> MPD_DB=postgres:18
#       Checks the value, writes the line, and applies the change.
#
#   Edit this file by hand, then run: mpd start <project>
#       Accepts any value. The second command is what applies it.
#
# mpd wrote this file when you ran `mpd init` and will never overwrite
# it. Git ignores it.
#
# Where defaults come from and which file wins when two disagree:
# docs/architecture.md, section 8.


# Database
#
# Astro builds static sites and needs no database, so this is empty.
#
# Keep it empty. The value is doing work: an empty setting here overrides
# any MPD_DB you set for all your projects in
# /var/lib/mpd/env/mpd-virt.env, which would otherwise give this project a
# database it never uses.
MPD_DB=""


# The dev-server port is not set here
#
# Set it in astro.config.mjs as `server.port`, then run
# `mpd start <project>`. mpd reads the port from there and points caddy
# at it. Astro uses 4321 when you set nothing.
#
# There is deliberately no setting for it in this file. mpd does not start
# the dev server, so a port named here could only move caddy — the server
# would keep binding whatever astro.config.mjs says, and the two would
# disagree.
#
# Give two Astro projects on one VM different ports. The second one to
# start cannot bind an address the first already holds.
